{"Title":"An Act stimulating small business investment","BillNumber":"S1805","DocketNumber":"SD1612","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T20:16:33.44"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T20:16:33.44"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1805/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Fattman, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1805) of Ryan C. Fattman for legislation to stimulate small business investment.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 63 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after section 38HH the following section:-\r\n\tSection 38II. A business corporation shall be allowed a credit against its tax liability imposed under this chapter equal to not more than the first $500,000 of revenue earned by said corporation during the taxable year for which the tax is due. The credit allowed by this section shall not reduce the excise to an amount less than the amount due under subsection (b) of section 39 of this chapter.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}